istical significance of the regression coefficients.\n\nTo detect heteroskedasticity, several tests can be employed, including the Breusch-Pagan test and the White test. If heteroskedasticity is detected, remedial measures can be taken, such as transforming the dependent variable, using weighted least squares, or applying robust standard errors to correct for the inefficiency of the OLS estimators.\n\nIn summary, homoskedasticity is a critical assumption in regression analysis that ensures the constancy of error variance across observations. Its validity is essential for the efficiency of OLS estimators and the reliability of statistical inferences. Understanding and testing for homoskedasticity is vital for econometric analysis, as violations can significantly impact the conclusions drawn from regression models.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": [], "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "protected_material_code": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "protected_material_text": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "violence": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}}}], "created": 1771166104, "model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": "fp_f97eff32c5", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 527, "prompt_tokens": 299, "total_tokens": 826, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0}}, "prompt_filter_results": [{"prompt_index": 0, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "jailbreak": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": f